The Path Pane displays the current path for the base window.  You can use the glyphs in this pane to "Open" a new directory higher up in the path or to change properties of the directories in the path.  Double clicking SELECT is the quick way to "open" a new directory.  An alternative mechanism involves SELECTing a directory and then using the MENU button to pop-up the Path Commands Menu.

The Path Commands MENU has buttons which can be used to "Open" the SELECTed directory  or to change its "Properties".

The "Open" button causes the File Manager to change the working directory to the selected directory and display its contents.

"Properties" brings up the file property window to allow changes to the directory name, the owner name, the group name, and permissions on the directory.
